.policy "ruff-ret507-superfluous-else-continue" revision 2
.description "Remove the else or elif after an if branch that continues the loop, and dedent its code; the branch already skips ahead."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff RET507 (flake8-return): an `elif` or `else` right after an `if` body whose first jump is a `continue`. That
// branch goes on to the next iteration, so the rest can be dedented. Only an if's first elif/else clause is
// paired with its body, and only the body's own statements are looked at, in order: the first return, raise,
// break or continue decides which rule fires. Checked in each def RET reads (python/flow-return); reported
// at the keyword.
//   if x:
//       continue
//   else:                      ← RET507 "Unnecessary `else` after `continue` statement"
//       y()
#include "python/flow-return.rr"

.violation RET507(at: span, w: symbol) code "RET507" "Unnecessary `{w}` after `continue` statement"
    suppress ruff "RET507"
RET507(kw, w) :- else_after_jump(kw, w, "continue").
